<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Montserrat" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" />
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="Montserrat, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text font-size="15px" color="#333333" line-height="1.7" align="justify" />
    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-preview>Three ways to connect Salesforce to Power BI, and the trade-offs no one tells you upfront.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#f4f4f4" width="640px">

    <!-- Header banner -->
    <mj-section padding="0">
      <mj-column padding="0">
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/newsletter/header.png" width="640px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="40px 40px 30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="34px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.2" align="center">
          Salesforce Power BI Integration: Choose the Right Approach
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Sponsor block — Metrica (external) -->
    <mj-section background-color="#e9f5f7" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="15px" color="#142328" padding-bottom="8px">
          Brought to you by:
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="16px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" padding-bottom="12px">
          Metrica Power BI Connector for Salesforce
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="justify" font-size="14px" color="#142328" padding-top="4px">
          Connect Salesforce data to Power BI without building a custom pipeline. Define your data sources inside Salesforce, let the connector handle pagination and incremental refresh, and reuse the same datasets across every report your team builds.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="justify" font-size="14px" color="#142328">
          Available on Salesforce AgentExchange. Initial setup can be completed in a single day.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://metricasoftware.com/power-bi-connector-for-salesforce/?utm_source=bibb-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=N0016" align="center" background-color="#FF0020" color="#ffffff" width="200px">
          Learn more
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Oscar's Take -->
    <mj-section background-color="#f9f9f9" padding="30px 40px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" font-weight="bold" color="#FF0020" letter-spacing="2px" padding-bottom="12px">
          OSCAR'S TAKE
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation">
            <tr>
              <td style="padding-right:14px;vertical-align:middle;">
                <img src="https://bibb.pro/images/authors/oscar-martinez.png" width="56" height="56" style="border-radius:50%;display:block;" alt="Oscar" />
              </td>
              <td style="vertical-align:middle;">
                <div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#142328;line-height:1.4;">Oscar Martinez</div>
                <div style="font-size:13px;color:#888888;line-height:1.4;">Editor, bibb Newsletter</div>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#f9f9f9" padding="0 40px 30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>
          Right now, I am going through a strong transition period on several fronts at once, 
          where things are shifting faster than I can document them. In the middle of all of it, 
          one of the things I am genuinely grateful for is the network I have built over the years. 
          People who pick up the call, open a door, or simply show up when it matters.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/antonstorozhuk/" style="color:#FF0020;">Anton Storozhuk</a> is one of those people. 
          We met years ago, drifted apart the way you do when careers take you in different directions, and reconnected recently. 
          He is the Founder and CEO of <a href="https://metricasoftware.com/?utm_source=bibb-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=N0016" style="color:#FF0020;">Metrica Software</a>. 
          When we first discussed bringing to bibb an article discussing Salesforce integration, for me it was a no-brainer: 
          I have worked in and for several Salesforce-heavy organisations, so I know the integration problem he describes is 
          real, and it hurts. And having worked with Anton before, I know the depth he brings to solving it.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          If you have tried to connect Salesforce to Power BI, you know the problem. 
          The native connector works until the data volume breaks it. 
          A custom pipeline gives you control but also a second job.
           Anton's guide maps the real trade-offs across three integration approaches, 
           with enough detail to be useful the next time someone drops "can we pull this from Salesforce?" in a meeting.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Featured this week: his practical comparison guide. Bookmark it, and send it to whoever owns your Salesforce reporting setup.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-social font-size="12px" icon-size="22px" mode="horizontal" align="left" padding-top="8px" padding-bottom="0">
          <mj-social-element src="https://www.mailjet.com/images/theme/v1/icons/ico-social/linkedin.png" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/oscarmartinezv/" background-color="#0077b5" padding="4px" />
          <mj-social-element name="youtube" href="https://www.youtube.com/@bibb_pro" background-color="#FF0020" padding="4px" />
        </mj-social>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#e0e0e0" border-width="1px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Featured post card -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/blog/heros/salesforce-power-bi-integration-right-approach.png" href="https://bibb.pro/post/salesforce-power-bi-integration-right-approach/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=N0016&utm_content=image-post" border-radius="6px" padding-bottom="16px" />
        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.3" padding-bottom="8px">
          Salesforce Power BI Integration: A Practical Comparison Guide
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555">
          Three approaches to connecting Salesforce with Power BI, compared across data volume, governance, and operational ownership. Native connectors, custom API pipelines, and the Metrica connector, each with a clear breakdown of when to use which and what it costs you long-term.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://bibb.pro/post/salesforce-power-bi-integration-right-approach/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=N0016&utm_content=cta-post" align="left" padding-top="10px" padding-bottom="6px" background-color="#FF0020">
          Go to featured post
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-social font-size="12px" icon-size="22px" mode="horizontal" align="left" padding-bottom="10px">
          <mj-social-element src="https://www.mailjet.com/images/theme/v1/icons/ico-social/linkedin.png" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/bibb" background-color="#0077b5" />
        </mj-social>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" color="#aaaaaa" line-height="1.6">
          © 2026 bibb PowerPivot Digital Communities<br />
          This e-mail has been sent to [[EMAIL_TO]], <a href="[[UNSUB_LINK_EN]]" style="color:#aaaaaa;text-decoration:none;">click here to unsubscribe</a>.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
